    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In &quot;<strong>Ball Torment</strong>,&quot; you steer NekoChan, the waifu you never wanted but now need, through a relentless barrage of balls on ramps. <br>If this simple task overwhelms you, you're not cut out to be called a gamer - you're just an onlooker. <br>If you can't dominate this game, you might as well log off your Steam account for good because real gamers don't just play Ball Torment, they master it.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>What to expect?</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Expect an extremely challenging game where you must dodge balls as you run up the ramps to open the doors to pass to the next stage.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >As a physics based game your momentum can be a blessing and a curse.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Each stage adds new balls to the mix and increases the difficulty of completion.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Gameplay.<br><br>The gameplay is running... I don't know Steam has made me rewrite this section 3 times now, saying this isn't specific enough. <br>WASD controls.<br>You can crouch.<br>You can look around with the mouse.<br><br>Balls can knock you back, inhibit your movement and twist gravity to throw you around the stage.<br>If you fall off you respawn at the checkpoint.<br>There is no Save feature so you close the game and reopen it you will start from the beginning.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><br><strong>Future plans.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >We plan on adding hard mode and challenge runs in the future but this will happen as a free addon and any subsequent updates will be added to the base game and require no additional purchase.</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In &quot;<strong>Ball Torment</strong>,&quot; you steer NekoChan, the waifu you never wanted but now need, through a relentless barrage of balls on ramps. <br>If this simple task overwhelms you, you're not cut out to be called a gamer - you're just an onlooker. <br>If you can't dominate this game, you might as well log off your Steam account for good because real gamers don't just play Ball Torment, they master it.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>What to expect?</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Expect an extremely challenging game where you must dodge balls as you run up the ramps to open the doors to pass to the next stage.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >As a physics based game your momentum can be a blessing and a curse.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Each stage adds new balls to the mix and increases the difficulty of completion.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Gameplay.<br><br>The gameplay is running... I don't know Steam has made me rewrite this section 3 times now, saying this isn't specific enough. <br>WASD controls.<br>You can crouch.<br>You can look around with the mouse.<br><br>Balls can knock you back, inhibit your movement and twist gravity to throw you around the stage.<br>If you fall off you respawn at the checkpoint.<br>There is no Save feature so you close the game and reopen it you will start from the beginning.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><br><strong>Future plans.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >We plan on adding hard mode and challenge runs in the future but this will happen as a free addon and any subsequent updates will be added to the base game and require no additional purchase.</p>",
